SU3HOB-ladder -- file manifest

  README             this description
  LICENSE            MIT license
  MANIFEST           this file
  Makefile           all / check / bench / clean

  hob_su3.f90        SU(3)-basis HOB engine; isofactors from the U(2)
                     pseudo-spin ladder (kernel of J+ plus lowering)
  WignerSymbol.f90   SU(2) Clebsch-Gordan coefficients; bundled unmodified
                     from https://github.com/0382/WignerSymbol (MIT)
  tmb_kam.f90        classical Talmi-Moshinsky bracket: the compact expression
                     of Kamuntavicius et al. (2001), with the 6j, 9j and
                     Clebsch-Gordan coefficients of Varshalovich et al.;
                     the independent reference of the validation driver
  hob.f90            command-line front end
  test_hob_su3.f90   validation driver
  test_hob_su3.ref   expected numerical output of the validation driver

  bench/ladder.f90   per-shell timing and orthonormality sweep

  .gitignore         build products, LaTeX intermediates and doc/

  logs/              the measurement logs behind every table of the article:
    ladder_vs_vcs_E50.log
        per-shell timings and orthonormality for the two isofactor routes
        (ladder and VCS), E <= 50.  Tables 2 and 3.
    ladder_vs_kam01_E32.log
        per-shell prepare/evaluate times for the ladder route and the
        classical route tmb_kam, with the largest element-wise deviation
        between them, E <= 32.  Tables 2 and 3, and the cost fits.
    cfp_ladder_vs_kam01_E30.log
        three-particle CFPs: departure of the eigenvalues of Lambda from the
        exact integers, both routes, E <= 30.  Table 6.
    shell_totals_and_diag_E50.log
        per-shell block count, largest block, bracket count sum_L n_L^2,
        prepare+evaluate time and running total over every block with
        E <= 50; then the CFP diagonalization time per shell.  The Program
        summary running time, the diagonalization column of Table 6, and
        the bracket-count fit of Eq. (17).
    classical_routes_E30.log
        the same classical formula evaluated from tabulated binomial
        coefficients rather than logarithms (the published HOTB C6J route
        and the variant using Tuzun's x6j_opt), E <= 30.  This is the
        evidence for Table 5: it is kept because the article contrasts the
        two tabulations, although neither of those codes is distributed
        here.

  The derivation of the ladder construction and the accompanying program
  article are not distributed with the source tree; see the ACCOMPANYING
  ARTICLE section of README.
